  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Perimeter Solutions has $343M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 20 awards with an average award size of $17.1M. Perimeter Solutions' obligations are up 7.5% year over year. Perimeter Solutions' fiscal-year obligations have risen from $164M in FY21, to $106M in FY22, to $89.9M in FY23, then climbed to $248M in FY24 and $319M in FY25 before reaching $343M in FY26. Perimeter Solutions' largest federal buyers in FY2026 to date are the Department of Agriculture at $227M and the Department of the Interior at $116M. Perimeter Solutions' current-year totals are fiscal year to date and represent partial-year obligations. Perimeter Solutions recorded 20 awards this fiscal year, and the average award size across those awards is $17.1M. Perimeter Solutions' year-over-year change is up 7.5%. This snapshot shows where Perimeter Solutions is concentrated by agency and how obligations have evolved across fiscal years, providing a concise picture of federal dependency and recent momentum for sales to the government.",
    "sections": [
